WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.350
Let's get into audience questions for the
weekend.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.350
Very good.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.350
Yeah.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.230
This week, the first one comes from a reddit
user.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.080
I never say this right.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.080
Nostalgic.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.270
Say in Cyan [inaudible].

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.350
I know it's some video game game thing and
I never know how to say it.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:20.010
Anyway, the question is how come the left
doesn't have grifters like the right, I love

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.300
this question because there's actually a lot
to it.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.570
It might sound like an ad Hominem.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.590
It's a way to criticize right-wingers.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:28.040
Listen, this is a real thing.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:35.430
The right has these grifters who able to,
they suffer from audience capture where they

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:40.600
start modifying what it is that they put out
there in order to appeal to an audience, even

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:47.040
if these are not really their political beliefs,
but that would only work within or in front

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.220
of a certain audience because of the cults
of personality, the right rewards.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:56.260
This is one of the big differences between
independent left-wing media and independent

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:57.260
right-wing media.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.540
I've seen it myself.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:05.489
I can have people who like 95% of what I say
and as soon as they don't like some 5%, I

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:07.400
say, Oh, you know what?

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.409
I don't think Tulsi Gabber is a great president.

00:01:09.409 --> 00:01:10.720
Or Hey, you know what?

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:18.420
I think the squad lacks a lot of the political,
uh, skills to, um, make progress on some of

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:19.880
these issues that are important to them.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.159
Or, Hey, you know what?

00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:25.619
I don't think Israel is a uniquely blood lusting
bad actor.

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:30.249
While I do disagree with their administration
and their foreign policy, there is no cult

00:01:30.249 --> 00:01:33.860
of personality around me because immediately
people who have been with me for years will

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.920
completely abandoned me.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.990
Now we can talk about whether that's good
or bad for the movement, but with the right

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:45.680
you see cults of personality develop such
that these individuals can do no wrong.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:51.619
They build a following for their personality,
not what they stand for, not what they believe

00:01:51.619 --> 00:01:57.880
and not what they say, but for the sort of
role that they are given by the right.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:04.829
The left both doesn't allow these grifters
to build around cults of personality and is

00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:10.399
quite frankly not interested in them in the
same way we've talked before about how you

00:02:10.399 --> 00:02:15.180
will see very different reactions from left
and right when there is a political scandal

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.180
ones.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.150
I'm not talking about Hillary's emails, right?

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:23.620
I'm talking about actual scandals, the right,
we'll try to cover them up and make excuses

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:29.090
for the people and try to make the scandal
go away to keep the person in power or even

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.130
give them more power.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:34.530
As we saw with Brett Kavanaugh on the left,
when we find out Anthony Wiener has been caught

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.820
sexting with a 15 year old or whatever, people
just want them out.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:38.820
We want to move on.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:43.590
We have ideas and principles and policies
that we want to see made a reality.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:48.010
And as soon as we see that somebody is behaving
in a way that doesn't make sense, we want

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:49.010
them out.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:54.250
There was this audio recording that was recently
covered up by Republicans in Texas where a

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:59.140
Republican came up with a Republican Hitlist
of Republicans to primary and Republican said

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.790
this, the recording of this conversation is
so damaging.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.160
We've got to cover it up.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.511
If I found out that someone on the left took
place in such a meeting and I found it, that

00:03:06.511 --> 00:03:11.580
the, and I found it distasteful or disadvantageous,
I would want the audio tape out.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.550
I would want to figure out who did the wrong
thing and I would want them out.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:24.600
So again, um, the, the, the left simply doesn't
allow the grifting to become profitable the

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.790
way the right does.

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:30.040
It doesn't create an environment in which
one would succeed by doing that.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.940
Now I know I'm not stupid.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:36.560
I know half the youtube comments will be,
but David, you are a grifter.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.850
That's not an actual argument.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.150
I hope you understand.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:46.310
Um, it is the audiences that decide whether
grifting will work on the left or on the right.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:51.740
It is the audiences that decide can someone
build a career around a cult of personality

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:55.010
merely because some think tank is pumping
money into them and what you see is that the

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:58.230
answers are yes on the right and mostly no
on the left.

